  "notes": "RedPeak Properties: full portfolio pulled from https://redpeak.com/search-all-redpeak/ (server-rendered, worked well). All 47 properties live only on redpeak.com/property/* pages -- no separate community domains were found (checked several individual property pages, e.g. /property/story/), so all are own_domain:false. Zocalo Community Development: pulled from https://zocalodevelopment.com/property-management-services/, all communities live on zocalodevelopment.com/project/* (own_domain:false). Legacy Partners: the https://legacypartners.com/communities/ page is an interactive/filterable search widget that returned no listings via WebFetch (JS-driven, and a ?state=CO query param returned 404) -- had to reconstruct via WebSearch. Found 4 CO communities with confirmed own-domain marketing sites (Legacy at Fitz, Araceli DTC, Legacy on the Promenade, Fox Crossing -- note Fox Crossing was sold in 2019 to Avanath but legacypartners.com still lists Legacy as manager). Excluded Westlake Greens (Littleton) because current listings show it now managed by Willow Bridge Property Company, not Legacy Partners. Holland Partner Group / Holland Residential: hollandresidential.com homepage and /projects page render as a JS carousel with almost no listing text via WebFetch; had to use WebSearch/individual URLs. Found Platform at Union Station, The Deveraux, and Union Denver as pages on hollandresidential.com/co/denver/* (own_domain:false, and Union Denver's status is uncertain -- one Yelp listing tags it CLOSED) plus Kallisto at Bear Creek which has its own confirmed domain (kallistoatbearcreek.com). Lincoln Property Company (CO): lpc.com/properties/ is JS-only and returned no CO multifamily listings; residential division was rebranded to Willow Bridge Property Company in 2023 (separate operator, out of scope for this batch), so no communities recorded for Lincoln Property Company. BMC Investments: full list pulled from https://www.bmcinv.com/multifamily-acquisition and https://www.bmcinv.com/multifamily-development (both rendered fine). Note BMC sold its property-management division to Asset Living in 2023 -- BMC still owns these assets per its own site but day-to-day management may be Asset Living; all links are bmcinv.com/* pages (own_domain:false). Nichols Partnership: pulled from https://nicholspartnership.com/projects-category/residential-villas/; excluded SPIRE (for-sale condominiums, not apartments) and Manor Homes at Cherry Creek (appears to be for-sale, unverified as rental) to avoid false positives. Palisade Partners: homepage projects (Arrowleaf, The Glade, Summit Sky Ranch, Overlook) are for-sale/mountain-town townhome projects, not rental apartments, so excluded; kept only the three confirmed Denver rental apartment projects (Luma, Oso, Ayden). Confluence Companies: portfolio paginated across https://www.confluenceco.com/portfolio/ pages 1-3; excluded The Eddy (boutique hotel) and Encore (for-sale condominiums in Castle Rock); several smaller projects (East Main, The Col, Rivertown, Union West, North Main at Steel Ranch, West 8th, Riverwalk Castle Rock, 1750 Jackson) had no separate marketing domain found on their confluenceco.com project pages, so marketing_url is set to that project page with own_domain:false. McWhinney: mcwhinney.com/portfolio/ repeatedly returned HTTP 429 (rate limited) via WebFetch; reconstructed via WebSearch instead, finding 4 confirmed CO apartment communities with their own marketing domains. Aimco / AIR Communities: Aimco (AIV) spun off its stabilized multifamily portfolio into AIR Communities in Dec 2020 and is currently in a shareholder-approved plan of sale/liquidation (as of Feb 2026) with only a handful of development-stage assets remaining and no clear public list of named CO communities found. AIR Communities (aircommunities.com), headquartered in Denver, holds the bulk of the named, stabilized Colorado apartment portfolio and its community list page rendered cleanly with real per-property marketing domains, so that list is recorded here under this operator with a note that it is the Aimco successor entity, not the current Aimco/AIV itself. Littleton Capital Partners: this entity moved to Denver in 2015, renamed to LCP Development, with sister company LCP Management (lcpmanagement.net) -- both operate a portfolio of office/retail/industrial assets, not apartment communities; no qualifying apartment portfolio (3+ named communities) was found, so no communities recorded for this operator. No securecafe.com/rentcafe.com/appfolio.com/etc vendor-hosted leasing portals were fetched or parsed at any point; only operator- and property-owned marketing pages were used as sources.",
